  "notModeled": [
    "analog inputs and reference; the result is always the 0 V differential code (offset binary 0x200 on both buses)",
    "DF/DCS is a four-state analog-level strap (VA or float: offset binary; AGND or VRM: 2's complement, 0 V = 0x000) also selecting the clock duty-cycle stabilizer; listed in analog, the model always outputs offset binary",
    "OEB: the clocked bus has a single output enable, so OEA gates both DA and DB buses; OEB (DB0-DB9 high-Z when high) is not modeled",
    "MULTIPLEX pin: only the parallel mode (MULTIPLEX low) is modeled; multiplexed mode (A and B data alternating on DA0-DA9 with ABb) is not; ABb is never driven",
    "pipeline latency 7 clocks (7.5/8 in multiplexed mode) is not modeled (the code is constant)",
    "power-down exit time (1 us), clock frequency (15-65 MHz) and duty-cycle limits",
    "tDIS/tEN are typical values only (10 ns)",
    "digital inputs are referenced to VD (3.0-3.6 V), outputs to VDR (2.4 V to VD); vcc is the union"
